# Windows batch files MUST keep CRLF. cmd.exe mis-parses an LF-only .bat —
# it drops the first characters of lines, producing errors like
# "'tlocal' is not recognized as an internal or external command" from
# `setlocal`. This bit the TV build script once already.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# A systemd unit copied from a Windows checkout to a Linux box must not carry CRs.
*.service text eol=lf
# The TV bench scripts run in Git Bash / on the box: a CR at a line end breaks them.
tools/tv-bench/**/*.sh text eol=lf
